# PMS — Query & mutate

Wire Nest → PMS in three layers. Do not collapse them.

| Layer                 | Owns                                                                                           |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/lib/api` helpers | Thin `api.*` wrappers; return unwrapped `T`; browser paths without `/staff` (proxy injects it) |
| Query keys            | `src/lib/api/query-keys.ts` — `as const` tuples; one key (or factory) per resource             |
| Screens / forms       | `useQuery` / `useInfiniteQuery` / `useMutation`, cache updates, toasts, RHF `setError`         |

Client / envelope / credentials: [`pms-api.mdc`](pms-api.mdc). GET loading UX: [`pms-ui.mdc`](pms-ui.mdc). BE field-error shape: [`api-http.mdc`](api-http.mdc).

## Queries

```ts
useQuery({ queryKey: staffAdminsQueryKey, queryFn: listAdmins });
```

- Import keys + helpers from `@/lib/api` (barrel). Do not invent inline key strings in pages.
- Auth session probes: `retry: false`. Login-page probe: `staffSession({ skipUnauthorizedRedirect: true })`.
- Defaults live in `src/lib/query-client.ts` (staleTime 30s; no refetch-on-focus; never retry 4xx `ApiError`; mutations `retry: false`). Override only when the screen needs it.
- Unpaginated list / detail GET UI: Skeleton + `QueryRetryButton` → `refetch` (`pms-ui`).

## Infinite lists (offset `Paginated<T>`)

Nest lists return `{ items, pageInfo }` (`Paginated` / `PageInfo` in `@cabin/api-contract`). Use `useInfiniteQuery` — not page-number UI.

```ts
useInfiniteQuery({
  queryKey: staffPropertiesQueryKey(filters), // filters in key so q/status reset pages
  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => listProperties({ page: pageParam, ...filters }),
  initialPageParam: INFINITE_INITIAL_PAGE, // 1
  getNextPageParam: getNextPageParamFromPageInfo,
});
```

| Rule       | Detail                                                                                                                           |
| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Page param | 1-based `page`; next = `page < totalPages ? page + 1 : undefined` via `getNextPageParamFromPageInfo`                             |
| Query keys | Factories include list filters (`q`, `status`, …). Invalidate with the **list** prefix tuple after writes                        |
| Flatten    | `data.pages.flatMap((p) => p.items)`                                                                                             |
| Scroll UX  | Shared [`InfiniteListFooter`](../../apps/pms/src/components/infinite-list-footer.tsx) + `react-intersection-observer` (`pms-ui`) |

**Errors (do not conflate):**

| Failure                          | Keep loaded pages? | Retry                                       |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| Page 1 (`isError` && no `data`)  | N/A                | `refetch`                                   |
| Page 2+ (`isFetchNextPageError`) | **Yes**            | `fetchNextPage()` — same failed `pageParam` |

On next-page error: **unmount the in-view sentinel** and show footer + `QueryRetryButton`. Leaving the sentinel `inView` while errored causes an auto-fetch loop.

## Mutations & cache (locked)

### Decision: `setQueryData` vs `invalidateQueries`

| Situation                                                                    | Do                                                                        |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Mutation response is **1:1 with a GET detail** (same `Staff*` row)           | `setQueryData(detailKey, saved)` — **do not** refetch that detail         |
| Unpaginated list you can patch locally (e.g. `StaffAdmin[]`)                 | Merge/`setQueryData` the list from `saved` — no list GET                  |
| Infinite / filtered / board lists (membership or sort may change)            | `invalidateQueries({ queryKey: *List*Prefix })` — server recomputes pages |
| Related derived data (availability, occupancy, parent counts)                | Invalidate **only** those prefixes when the write can change them         |
| Delete / no usable body / logout                                             | Invalidate (or `removeQueries`) — nothing to write                        |
| Stale risk matters more than a round-trip (boards, busy nights after cancel) | Prefer invalidate for that slice — correctness over chatter               |

**Never** invalidate a broad resource prefix that also matches the detail key you just `setQueryData`’d — use a `…ListQueryKeyPrefix` (or tighter) so detail stays from the mutation.

### Helpers (use these — don’t invent ad-hoc invalidates)

| Write                                        | Helper                                                                             |
| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Reservation ops returning `StaffReservation` | `syncReservationCaches(qc, saved, { occupancyChanged? })`                          |
| Property create/update                       | `syncPropertyCaches(qc, saved)`                                                    |
| Unit type create/update                      | `syncUnitTypeCaches(qc, saved)`                                                    |
| Unit create/update                           | `syncUnitCaches(qc, saved, { bookabilityChanged? })`                               |
| Staff admin create/role/active               | `syncStaffAdminCaches(qc, saved)`                                                  |
| Inventory **delete** / tree wipe             | `invalidateInventoryCaches(qc)`                                                    |
| Calendar block create/update/delete          | `invalidatePropertyCalendarCaches(qc)` — aggregate has no block detail key         |
| iCal Sync all                                | `invalidateIcalSyncCaches(qc)` — full cache (stubs / occupancy / calendar / feeds) |
| Login / change username                      | `setQueryData(staffSessionQueryKey, admin)`                                        |
| Logout                                       | `invalidateQueries(staffSessionQueryKey)` then `/login`                            |

**Where cache helpers live**

| Pattern                                              | Put helper                                                                                                                                                                             |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| One resource module (reservations, admins, calendar) | Same file as that resource’s HTTP helpers (`reservations.ts`, `admins.ts`, `calendar.ts`)                                                                                              |
| Shared across several inventory HTTP files           | `inventory-cache.ts`                                                                                                                                                                   |
| Naming                                               | `sync*Caches` when mutation body maps 1:1 to a GET detail (`setQueryData` + targeted invalidates); `invalidate*Caches` when there is nothing to write (delete, aggregate-only refresh) |

Do **not** name helpers `*Queries`. Do **not** call `invalidateQueries` with ad-hoc key strings from screens — export a helper and list it in this table.

`occupancyChanged` / `bookabilityChanged`: only when unit nights or bookability can change (create, date/unit move, checkout, cancel, unit status). Skip for money-only, confirm, check-in, guest/notes edits. Reservation sync **always** invalidates the property calendar prefix (stay bars paint status / Late / money, not only busy nights).

Always `handleSuccess` in mutation `onSuccess` — never in the axios interceptor.

### Success — clear local state first (locked)

TanStack `mutation.isPending` flips **false** when the request settles. `onOpenChange(false)` / dialog unmount runs on the **next** render. In that gap, submit buttons re-enable while the shell is still open — rapid clicks can fire a **second** write.

**Every** `useMutation` `onSuccess` in PMS: **clear local UI state first**, then cache sync, toast, navigate, or close.

| Local state                  | Clear first (examples)                                                                                                |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| RHF form                     | `form.reset(emptyFormValues())` — reuse a module-level `emptyFormValues` / `emptyDefaults`; not ad-hoc partial clears |
| Choose-unit / picker         | Three-state: `undefined` = fall back to reservation / `initialChosen`; `null` = cleared; object = pick. See below.   |
| Picker open                  | `setPickerOpen(false)`                                                                                                |
| Dialog / sheet open          | `onOpenChange(false)` or `setXOpen(false)` **after** reset                                                            |
| Delete confirm               | `setDeleteTarget(null)`                                                                                               |
| Ops confirm (check-in, etc.) | `setPendingPrimary(null)`                                                                                             |
| Staff re-auth                | `closeReauth()` / `setPending(null)`                                                                                  |
| Media uploading flags        | `setMediaUploading(false)`                                                                                            |
| Login / settings             | `form.reset(…)` + hide-password toggles before navigate / close                                                       |

**Choose-unit `picked` on success** (when `chosen = picked !== undefined ? picked : reservation \| initialChosen`):

| Moment | Set | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create success (shell may stay open for OTA remind) | `setPicked(null)` | Avoid falling back to `initialChosen` while the empty form is still mounted |
| Edit / confirm-enrich success | `setPicked(undefined)` | Stay-mounted dialogs (e.g. detail Edit) must fall back to the reservation on reopen — `null` sticks as “No unit” |
| Mid-session hard clear (unit not bookable) | `setPicked(null)` | Intentionally empty until staff picks again |
| Cancel / close via `handleOpenChange(false)` | `setPicked(undefined)` | Drop local override |

```ts
onSuccess: (saved) => {
  form.reset(emptyFormValues());
  setPicked(isEdit || isConfirmEnrich ? undefined : null);
  setPickerOpen(false);
  syncReservationCaches(queryClient, saved, { occupancyChanged });
  handleSuccess("Reservation created");
  onOpenChange(false);
},
```

**Confirm dialogs** ([`confirm-dialog.tsx`](../../apps/pms/src/components/ui/confirm-dialog.tsx)):

- Confirm button calls `onConfirm()` only — **do not** `onOpenChange(false)` inside the dialog.
- Parent closes by clearing target state in `onSuccess` (or immediately for blocked “Got it” flows).
- Pass `confirmDisabled={mutation.isPending}` so confirm stays dead while the request runs.

**Re-auth** ([`reauth-password-dialog.tsx`](../../apps/pms/src/components/reauth-password-dialog.tsx)): reset password field in `onOpenChange(false)` (and Cancel); parent still clears `pending` in `onSuccess` first.

**Don’t**

- Rely on `isPending` alone to block double-submit on dialogs/sheets
- Add a submit-lock hook/latch as the default fix — clear state on success instead
- `setPicked(null)` on **edit** success when the dialog stays mounted — next Edit shows “No unit chosen”

## Errors — pick one path

| Failure                                                          | Handler                                                                                          |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Domain field error `details: { field, reason }`                  | `applyApiFieldError(error, form.setError)` — if it returns `true`, **do not** also `handleError` |
| Re-auth password dialog (`INVALID_CURRENT_PASSWORD`)             | Dialog `serverError` (or equivalent) — no toast                                                  |
| Login / auth / 404 / role / class-validator `string[]` / network | `handleError` → Sonner toast                                                                     |
| Delete blocked (`HAS_CHILDREN`)                                  | Dialog or toast — **not** RHF `setError`                                                         |
| Failed GET (page 1 / detail)                                     | Inline message + retry — **not** a toast storm                                                   |
| Failed infinite next page                                        | Footer retry via `fetchNextPage` — see above                                                     |

`applyApiFieldError` already toasts non-field errors. Callers that branch first (re-auth vs username) must not double-toast.

## Forms ↔ BE

- Zod mins/maxes/patterns from `@cabin/api-contract` — same bounds as Nest DTOs.
- Form property names **must** match DTO / `details.field` so highlight lands on the right input.
- UI: `Controller` + `<Field data-invalid={fieldState.invalid}>` + `<FieldError />`.
- New `ApiFieldReason` → add in `@cabin/api-contract` first; optional label in `FIELD_REASON_MESSAGE`.

## Don’t

- Toast inside axios interceptors
- Second axios instance / raw `fetch` to Nest
- Duplicate query-key literals outside `query-keys.ts`
- Refetch GET detail when the mutation already returned that same row
- Nuke all inventory prefixes after a single-entity update (use `sync*Caches`)
- `setError` for operational conflicts (`HAS_CHILDREN`) or login credential failures
- Optimistic UI unless the screen explicitly needs it
- Keep the infinite-scroll sentinel mounted while `isFetchNextPageError` (error loop)
